=== Second round ===
Former candidate of [[Sergio Fajardo]], leader of ''Movimiento Compromiso Ciudadano'', announced his blank vote for the second round,<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.semana.com/nacion/articulo/ni-petro-ni-duque-sergio-fajardo-anuncia-que-votara-en-blanco/569441 |title= Ni Petro, ni Duque: Sergio Fajardo anuncia que votará en blanco |access-date= 13 June 2018 |date=31 May 2018 |publisher= Semana |language= es}}</ref> as well as former liberal candidate [[Humberto de La Calle]], although his party joined Iván Duque's campaign.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.semana.com/nacion/articulo/humberto-de-la-calle-votara-en-blanco/569460 |title= Humberto de la Calle votará en blanco |access-date= 13 June 2018 |date=31 May 2018 |publisher= Semana |language=es}}</ref> The [[Alternative Democratic Pole]] joined Gustavo Petro's campaign, but a minority sector led by Senator Jorge Robledo (MOIR) decided to vote blank too.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.elespectador.com/noticias/politica/polo-democratico-se-decide-por-gustavo-petro-articulo-791718 |title=Polo Democrático se decide por Gustavo Petro |access-date= 13 June 2018 |date=31 May 2018 |publisher=El Espectador |language= es}}</ref> The directive of the [[Green Alliance (Colombia)|Green Alliance]] let their followers to choose between supporting Gustavo Petro or voting blank, but considered unacceptable to support Iván Duque.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.elespectador.com/elecciones-2018/noticias/politica/alianza-verde-convoca-votar-contra-duque-articulo-791852 |title= Alianza Verde convoca a votar contra Duque |access-date= 13 June 2018|date=31 May 2018 |publisher= El Espectador |language= es }}</ref> ''Movimiento Mejor Vargas Lleras'' and the [[Radical Change]] party sent their former candidate's program to Iván Duque, to consider it for a future government, although there was not an official adhesion.<ref>{{cite news |url= https://www.semana.com/nacion/articulo/cambio-radical-propone-alianza-con-el-centro-democratico-tras-derrota-de-vargas-lleras/569161 |title= Cambio Radical entrega a Duque el programa de gobierno de Vargas Lleras|access-date=13 June 2018 |date=28 May 2018 |publisher= Semana |language=es }}</ref> The ''Partido de la U''  and the [[Social Party of National Unity]] encouraged their followers choose freely to vote for their preferred option.<ref>{{cite news |url= http://www.elcolombiano.com/elecciones-2018-colombia/la-u-en-libertad-NL8782593 |title= Partido de la U deja en libertad a sus electores |access-date= 13 June 2018 |date=29 May 2018|publisher=El Colombiano |language=es }}</ref><ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.elheraldo.co/politica/la-asi-deja-en-libertad-su-militancia-de-cara-la-segunda-vuelta-505916 |title= La ASI deja en libertad a su militancia de cara a la segunda vuelta|access-date=13 June 2018 |date= 12 June 2018 |work=El Heraldo |language= es }}</ref>

